- deep-probe-max-tokens-too-small (lib/exploration.js:98): the tier 1 probe asks for max_tokens 400, a reasoning model spends it on thinking and the reply ends with finish length before the tool call, so the model fails the tier although it recalled all 3 facts. Seen in exploration.json for the three nemotron-3.5-lightning variants (recall 3, toolCall false, finish length); nemotron-3.5-lightning then served 2314 real requests with 53 failures.

    not reproduced from a script (no gateway key at hand); evidence is the cached deep results: recall 3, toolCall false, finish length

- deep-probe-transient-error-shown-as-context-lost (repl.js:3075): a tier 1 probe that failed with a rate limit (deep.error, deep.transient) is reported as k context failed, which events.js turns into context lost, and probeBrief shows 12k with a cross. 5 of the 9 failed deep results in exploration.json are electronhub rate limits (qwen3.8-27b, deepseek-v4-flash, gemma-4-26b-a4b-it, glm-4.7-flash, openai-gpt-6-luna), none says anything about the context window.

    /model health   (the probe column of qwen3.8-27b reads 12k with a cross)

- failed-request-rated-against-requested-name (repl.js:2938): a request that failed has no routedVia, so recordResult rates the failure against meta.requested: the pseudo model auto has 30 failures and 0 successes in ratings.json (adj -25), and a pinned name collects failures of the whole gateway. Harness side exceptions that surface as the request error (is not defined, not a function, unknown color: 12 of the 236 logged errors, 11 of them on nemotron-3.5-lightning) count as model failures too.

    note: see ratings.json and usage.jsonl in the cache directory

- usage-records-not-labelled (lib/persist.js:appendUsage, repl.js:2936): usage.jsonl has no label (main, explore, standby, sub), so exploration probes and real requests are mixed in every statistic. 73 of the 104 failures that are not interrupted are All models exhausted/rate-limited, and many of them look like probes of blocked models (inferred from the requested names and bursts of different models within seconds), so the failure rate of the user path cannot be told from the probes.

    note: compare requested and platform in usage.jsonl, probes come in bursts of different models within seconds

- rating-adj-saturates (lib/rating.js:30): the adjustment is capped at 25, so laguna-xs-2.1 (428 ok, 0 failed) and nemotron-3.5-lightning (2314 ok, 53 failed) and nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b both reach the cap and can no longer be told apart.

    note: see ratings.json, adj 25 for all three
- exit-change-uses-wrong-tor-host (repl.js:3292, repl.js:4331): the automatic exit change (autoExit) and /proxy exit call newExit() with no host, which falls back to TORHOST or 127.0.0.1, while the gateway's proxy is on another machine (socks5://192.168.178.52:9050 in the live session, TORHOST is not set), so NEWNYM goes to the wrong control port; only fixKeyless (repl.js:3506) passes the host taken from the socks URL.

    note: needs a proxy on another host to reproduce; compare newExit() calls with the one in fixKeyless

- rawcolor-test-expects-old-colors (test-rawcolor.js:39): 4 checks (colorMeta status green and 503 red, colorJson key teal, colorContent + line green) hard-code the old truecolor values (74;222;128, 248;113;113, 45;212;191) while rawcolor.js takes TEAL, GREEN, RED from palette.js (1f8181, 07923a, f83171), so they fail since the colors were changed; the code is fine, the test is stale.

